{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QC5twRcCfeMdMAXmCFAYrn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://github.com/cncf/curriculum/blob/master/KCNA_Curriculum.pdf\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation (cncf/curriculum)\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\"]\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-competencies\"]\n7\t---\n8\t# Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) Exam Curriculum — CNCF publication (text extracted from KCNA_Curriculum.pdf, 3 pages)\n9\t\n10\t\"This document provides the curriculum outline of the Knowledge, Skills and Abilities that a Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) can be expected to demonstrate.\"\n11\t\n12\t## KCNA Curriculum\n13\t- 44% – Kubernetes Fundamentals: Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization\n14\t- 28% – Container Orchestration: Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage\n15\t- 16% – Cloud Native Application Delivery: Application Delivery; Debugging\n16\t- 12% – Cloud Native Architecture: Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n17\t\n18\t(The PDF contains the typo \"Could Native Community and Collaboration\" for the last competency.)\n19\t\n20\t\"Cloud native computing uses an open source software stack to deploy applications as microservices, packaging each part into its own container, and dynamically orchestrating those containers to optimize resource utilization. The Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF) hosts critical components of those software stacks including Kubernetes, Fluentd, Linkerd, Prometheus, OpenTracing and gRPC; brings together the industry's top developers, end users, and vendors; and serves as a neutral home for collaboration. CNCF is part of The Linux Foundation, a nonprofit organization.\"\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c977363c-b218-4f47-91fb-e430a06317c3","uuid":"0645b2a9-c6a8-4d02-8d3d-8681ad63b943","timestamp":"2026-08-24T14:07:51.422Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/cncf-kcna-curriculum-pdf-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://github.com/cncf/curriculum/blob/master/KCNA_Curriculum.pdf\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T22:30:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation (cncf/curriculum)\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1\", \"D2\", \"D3\", \"D4\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-competencies\"]\n---\n# Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) Exam Curriculum — CNCF publication (text extracted from KCNA_Curriculum.pdf, 3 pages)\n\n\"This document provides the curriculum outline of the Knowledge, Skills and Abilities that a Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) can be expected to demonstrate.\"\n\n## KCNA Curriculum\n- 44% – Kubernetes Fundamentals: Kubernetes Core Concepts; Administration; Scheduling; Containerization\n- 28% – Container Orchestration: Networking; Security; Troubleshooting; Storage\n- 16% – Cloud Native Application Delivery: Application Delivery; Debugging\n- 12% – Cloud Native Architecture: Observability; Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles; Cloud Native Community and Collaboration\n\n(The PDF contains the typo \"Could Native Community and Collaboration\" for the last competency.)\n\n\"Cloud native computing uses an open source software stack to deploy applications as microservices, packaging each part into its own container, and dynamically orchestrating those containers to optimize resource utilization. The Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF) hosts critical components of those software stacks including Kubernetes, Fluentd, Linkerd, Prometheus, OpenTracing and gRPC; brings together the industry's top developers, end users, and vendors; and serves as a neutral home for collaboration. CNCF is part of The Linux Foundation, a nonprofit organization.\"\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QUg8MGiSVJSoYtsFshmhBj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://www.cncf.io/training/certification/kcna/\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation (cncf.io) — official KCNA certification page\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: []\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"cncf-certification-ladder\", \"kcna-exam-format\", \"domain-weights-44-28-16-12\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) — CNCF\n10\t\n11\t## Description and audience\n12\t\n13\t\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam demonstrates a user's foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem.\"\n14\t\n15\t\"The KCNA is a pre-professional certification designed for candidates interested in advancing to the professional level through a demonstrated understanding of kubernetes foundational knowledge and skills. This certification is ideal for students learning about or candidates interested in working with cloud native technologies.\"\n16\t\n17\t## Format and cost\n18\t\n19\t\"This exam is an online, proctored, multiple-choice exam.\"\n20\tCost: \"$250 and includes one free retake.\"\n21\t\n22\t## Certification ladder\n23\t\n24\t\"The KCNA exam is intended to prepare candidates to work with cloud native technologies and pursue further CNCF credentials, including CKA, CKAD, and CKS.\"\n25\t\n26\tCorroborated at https://www.cncf.io/training/certification/ : KCNA \"lays the\n27\tgroundwork for further CNCF certifications like CKA, CKAD, and CKS.\" That page\n28\tdescribes KCNA as \"online and multiple-choice\", CKA as a \"performance-based exam\n29\twhere candidates interact with the command line to solve real-world challenges\",\n30\tCKAD as a \"hands-on, command-line environment\", and CKS as \"performance-based\".\n31\t\n32\t## Domains\n33\t\n34\tKubernetes Fundamentals 44% · Container Orchestration 28% ·\n35\tCloud Native Application Delivery 16% · Cloud Native Architecture 12%\n36\t\n37\t## Not stated on this page\n38\t\n39\tDuration, question count, passing score, validity period, prerequisites.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c977363c-b218-4f47-91fb-e430a06317c3","uuid":"1ff27100-7b52-418e-8287-ec380cd526c3","timestamp":"2026-08-24T14:07:51.424Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/cncf-kcna-certification-page-2026-08-23.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://www.cncf.io/training/certification/kcna/\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-23T23:50:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Cloud Native Computing Foundation (cncf.io) — official KCNA certification page\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"cncf-certification-ladder\", \"kcna-exam-format\", \"domain-weights-44-28-16-12\"]\n---\n\n# Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) — CNCF\n\n## Description and audience\n\n\"The Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA) exam demonstrates a user's foundational knowledge and skills in Kubernetes and the wider cloud native ecosystem.\"\n\n\"The KCNA is a pre-professional certification designed for candidates interested in advancing to the professional level through a demonstrated understanding of kubernetes foundational knowledge and skills. This certification is ideal for students learning about or candidates interested in working with cloud native technologies.\"\n\n## Format and cost\n\n\"This exam is an online, proctored, multiple-choice exam.\"\nCost: \"$250 and includes one free retake.\"\n\n## Certification ladder\n\n\"The KCNA exam is intended to prepare candidates to work with cloud native technologies and pursue further CNCF credentials, including CKA, CKAD, and CKS.\"\n\nCorroborated at https://www.cncf.io/training/certification/ : KCNA \"lays the\ngroundwork for further CNCF certifications like CKA, CKAD, and CKS.\" That page\ndescribes KCNA as \"online and multiple-choice\", CKA as a \"performance-based exam\nwhere candidates interact with the command line to solve real-world challenges\",\nCKAD as a \"hands-on, command-line environment\", and CKS as \"performance-based\".\n\n## Domains\n\nKubernetes Fundamentals 44% · Container Orchestration 28% ·\nCloud Native Application Delivery 16% · Cloud Native Architecture 12%\n\n## Not stated on this page\n\nDuration, question count, passing score, validity period, prerequisites.\n","numLines":40,"startLine":1,"totalLines":40}}}
