{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cf2CXK51wRtx9MAFbBafiL","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Research Manifest — KCNA Chapter 7\n9:## Snapshots fetched\n21:### Already cached and verified adequate (no re-fetch needed)\n31:## Snapshots\n33:### A1 · `k8s-docs-topology-spread-constraints-2026-08-24.md` (new)\n45:# Pod Topology Spread Constraints (kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/topology-spread-constraints/)\n53:## What topology spread constraints are\n70:## Motivation\n97:## Node labels and topology\n109:## Field definitions\n111:### `maxSkew`\n128:### `topologyKey`\n135:### `whenUnsatisfiable`\n146:### `labelSelector`\n153:### `minDomains`\n161:### `matchLabelKeys`, `nodeAffinityPolicy`, `nodeTaintsPolicy`\n174:## Comparison with podAffinity and podAntiAffinity\n194:## Cluster-level default constraints\n203:## Known limitations\n239:### A2 · `k8s-docs-taints-tolerations-depth-2026-08-24.md` (new)\n252:# Taints and Tolerations — later sections (kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/taint-and-toleration/)\n262:## Command forms\n272:## Example Use Cases — Dedicated Nodes\n292:## Example Use Cases — Nodes with Special Hardware\n300:## How multiple taints are processed\n307:## `tolerationSeconds`\n315:## Empty key / `Exists` operator\n322:## Taint Nodes by Condition\n337:## Taint-based Evictions — built-in taints added by the node controller\n360:## Default tolerations added automatically\n368:## DaemonSet Pods\n387:### A3 · `k8s-docs-assign-pod-node-depth-2026-08-24.md` (new)\n400:# Assigning Pods to Nodes — depth (kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node/)\n406:## Node affinity `weight` (preferred rules)\n419:## How multiple terms and expressions combine\n433:## Inter-pod affinity and anti-affinity — `topologyKey`\n440:## Inter-pod affinity and anti-affinity — cost\n448:## Operator availability by affinity type\n457:## `nodeName`\n479:### A4 · `k8s-docs-pod-priority-preemption-2026